Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if time started moving backward?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.92,0:00:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Not in a laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.16,0:00:09.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Everywhere at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.35,0:00:13.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It starts with small things you almost don't notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.19,0:00:17.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Rain lifts off the pavement… and climbs back into the storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.90,0:00:21.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Spilled coffee flows up the table, back into the cup.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.97,0:00:26.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}A shattered glass pulls itself together on the kitchen floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.26,0:00:29.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In Tokyo, it is nine at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.45,0:00:32.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Cars glide backwards down the expressway.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.84,0:00:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In New York, it is breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.85,0:00:38.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Steam falls back into the street.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.50,0:00:43.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In Cape Town, birds fly tail-first over the harbour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.03,0:00:44.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Nobody is hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.94,0:00:46.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Nothing is broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.77,0:00:49.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Everything is simply going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.19,0:00:53.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And nobody on Earth can stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.94,0:00:56.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.32,0:00:59.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every river turns around in its bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.42,0:01:03.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one hour, the sea pulls back and does not return.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.61,0:01:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Ships lean over in the empty air where the water used to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.95,0:01:13.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one day, every tree takes its leaves back.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.31,0:01:17.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Petals climb off the grass, back onto the flowers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.41,0:01:22.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one week, broken buildings rise back into shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.27,0:01:27.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Concrete and glass fly upwards, and the dust goes with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.40,0:01:31.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one month, the cities go dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.77,0:01:36.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Eight billion people, moving backwards through their own lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.76,0:01:41.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one year, the deserts take back the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.71,0:01:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Sand moves uphill, and swallows the fences.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.79,0:01:49.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After ten years, everything we built is coming apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.86,0:01:52.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Towers come apart, floor by floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.89,0:01:57.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After a hundred years, the planet is what it was before us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.09,0:01:59.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Forests cover the roads.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.62,0:02:02.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Towers stand in the trees.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.33,0:02:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then comes the worst part.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.63,0:02:08.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Nothing new can ever happen again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.55,0:02:11.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every fire burns backwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.31,0:02:14.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every meal uncooks itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.06,0:02:17.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every chain of events runs backwards, step by step.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.90,0:02:21.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}There is nothing left to look forward to.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.86,0:02:24.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.99,0:02:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Time was never one single river.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.87,0:02:32.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In orbit, satellites already live in a slightly faster time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.37,0:02:36.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Their clocks gain about thirty-eight microseconds every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.60,0:02:39.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And it already happened to a man.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.43,0:02:43.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Sergei Krikalev spent eight hundred and three days in orbit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.62,0:02:47.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}He came home two hundredths of a second younger than the rest of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.16,0:02:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That is real time travel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.89,0:02:53.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}We just cannot feel it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.05,0:03:00.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So… if time really started going backwards… which day would you live again?
